**Question 1(i)**

Gap on each side of the plate:
$\frac{15-3}{2} = 6\text{ mm} = 0.006\text{ m}$ (matches the "Gap = 6mm" label).

Shear stress on each face (Newton's law of viscosity):

$$\tau = \mu \frac{V}{h}$$
$$= 1.5 \times \frac{0.15}{0.006} = 37.5 \text{ N/m}^2$$

Viscous force per face:

$$F_\tau = \tau A = 37.5 \times (0.8 \times 0.8) = 24 \text{ N}$$

Since there are two faces (both sides of the plate) and the plate moves at constant velocity, the applied force balances weight plus both viscous drag forces:

$$F = W + 2F_\tau = 110 + 2(24) = \boxed{158 \text{ N}}$$

