**Question 2**

*Reading of the figure:* radius $r = 1.25\text{ m}$, taking the cylinder centre $O$ as datum. Points $B$ (top), $C$ (left, level with $O$), $D$ (right, level with $O$), $A$ (bottom). Oil (SG 0.9) is in contact with the **entire left semicircle** ($B\to C\to A$), free surface $2.50\text{ m}$ above $O$. Liquid M (SG 0.8) is in contact with only the **lower-right quarter** ($D\to A$), free surface level with $O/D$. Per unit length ($L=1\text{ m}$), $\gamma_{oil}=8820\text{ N/m}^3$, $\gamma_M = 7840\text{ N/m}^3$.

**Horizontal components** (force on the vertical projection, at the centroid depth):

$$F_{H1} = \gamma_{oil}\,\bar h\,A_{proj} = 8820(2.50)(2.5\times1) = 55.13\text{ kN (→)}$$

$$F_{H2} = \gamma_M\,\bar h\,A_{proj} = 7840(0.625)(1.25\times1) = 6.13\text{ kN (←)}$$

**Vertical components** (weight of real/virtual liquid volume; for a full semicircular arc the horizontal strip terms cancel, leaving the buoyant volume of the arc itself):

$$F_{V1} = \gamma_{oil}\left(\frac{\pi r^2}{2}\right) = 8820\left(\frac{\pi (1.25)^2}{2}\right) = 21.65\text{ kN (↑)}$$

$$F_{V2} = \gamma_M\left(\frac{\pi r^2}{4}\right) = 7840\left(\frac{\pi (1.25)^2}{4}\right) = 9.62\text{ kN (↑)}$$

**Location of horizontal components above A** (centre of pressure of each vertical strip):

$$h_{cp,1} = \bar h + \frac{I_c}{\bar h A} \;\Rightarrow\; 1.04 \text{ m above } A$$
$$h_{cp,2} = \bar h + \frac{I_c}{\bar h A} \;\Rightarrow\; 0.42 \text{ m above } A$$

**Resultant force:**

$$\Sigma F_H = 55.13 - 6.13 = 49.0\text{ kN}, \qquad \Sigma F_V = 21.65+9.62 = 31.27\text{ kN}$$

$$R = \sqrt{49.0^2+31.27^2} = \boxed{58.14\text{ kN}}$$

$$\theta = \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{31.27}{49.0}\right) = \boxed{32.6^\circ \text{ above horizontal}}$$

Because every elemental pressure force on a circular arc acts radially, **the resultant passes through the centre $O$**, i.e. $1.25\text{ m}$ above $A$.

