**Question 3(i)**

Diagonal $d = a\sqrt2 = 0.6\sqrt2 = 0.8485\text{ m}$. Depth of centroid:

$$\bar h = 0.6 + \frac{d}{2} = 0.6+0.4243 = 1.0243\text{ m}$$

$$F = \gamma \bar h A = 9800(1.0243)(0.36) = \boxed{3.61\text{ kN}}$$

For a square, the second moment of area about **any** centroidal axis is the same regardless of orientation:

$$I_c = \frac{a^4}{12} = \frac{0.6^4}{12} = 0.0108\text{ m}^4$$

$$h_{cp} = \bar h + \frac{I_c}{\bar h A} = 1.0243 + \frac{0.0108}{(1.0243)(0.36)} = \boxed{1.054\text{ m below the surface}}$$

