**Question 3(ii)**

*Reading of the figure:* $A$ and $C$ (top of the dome) are separated by $3\text{ m}$ of water inside the closed tank. The piping loop from $A$ to $B$ rises $4\text{ m}$ through the SG $= 0.8$ liquid, then descends $3\text{ m} + 2\text{ m} = 5\text{ m}$ through water to $B$.

**Pressure at C** (going up 3 m in water from A):

$$P_C = P_A - \gamma_w(3) = 60 - 9.8(3) = \boxed{30.6\text{ kPa}}$$

Head in mm of mercury:

$$h = \frac{P_C}{\gamma_{Hg}} = \frac{30{,}600}{133{,}000} = 0.2301\text{ m} = \boxed{230.1\text{ mm Hg}}$$

**Pressure at B** (trace the piping loop):

$$P_B = P_A - \gamma_{0.8}(4) + \gamma_w(3) + \gamma_w(2)$$

$$P_B = 60 - 7.84(4) + 9.8(3) + 9.8(2) = 60 - 31.36 + 29.4+19.6 = \boxed{77.64\text{ kPa}}$$

