**Question 4**

Length of water added along the inclined tube:

$$L_2 = \frac{V}{a} = \frac{7.5}{0.5} = 15\text{ cm} \;\Rightarrow\; \text{vertical height} = 15\sin30^\circ = 7.5\text{ cm}$$

Let $h_1$ = rise in the vertical tube, $h_2$ = drop (vertical height) of the manometer-liquid interface in the inclined tube. Since the tube has uniform bore, conservation of manometer-liquid volume gives:

$$h_1 = \frac{h_2}{\sin30^\circ} = 2h_2 \quad (1)$$

Equating pressure at the junction from both limbs (both open to atmosphere):

$$\gamma_1(h_1+h_2) = \gamma_2(0.075) \quad (2)$$

Substituting (1) into (2), with $S_1=1.25,\ S_2=1.0$:

$$3h_2 = \frac{S_2}{S_1}(0.075) = 0.8(0.075) = 0.06$$

$$h_2 = 0.02\text{ m} = 2\text{ cm}$$

$$h_1 = 2h_2 = \boxed{4\text{ cm (0.04 m) rise in the vertical tube}}$$

